-- Ten machines two long-held books print and the catalog never held: eight
-- from Rifts Ultimate Edition and two from Pantheons of the Megaverse.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
-- Rifts Ultimate Edition (printed 249-254, 271-274): the UAR-1 Enforcer, the
-- CR-003 Spider-Skull Walker, the Mark V APC, the AFC-050 Death's Head
-- Transport, the AFC-023 Sky Cycle, the NG-X9 Samson, the FT-005 Flying Titan
-- and the TR-001 Titan Combat Robot. The book's rows accumulated across the
-- project rather than in one import, and its first inventory (2026-10-03, in
-- its survey) found these eight in neither `vehicles` nor `gear`.
-- Pantheons of the Megaverse (printed 106-107, 195): the Atlas Mark I assault
-- robot and the Ahriman Mark I Rune Assault Suit.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER WAS READ OFF A RENDER and checked against a render again by
-- book-reconcile: about 330 figures, none wrong. Every slug was queried
-- against production vehicles and gear before this file was written.
--
-- CONVENTIONS (as the Triax 2 and Warlords of Russia vessels):
--   cost is the lowest printed price; the full wording is in cost_note. "Not
--     available" is NULL with the wording kept (the Death's Head Transport).
--   Locations and weapons are in printed order, the Main Body among them.
--     Each numbered entry in the book is a weapon row with the book's number.
--   A book slip is stored as printed and named in the row: the Enforcer's and
--     Titan's single turrets printed "each", the Mark V's turret heading, the
--     Death's Head's two lengths, and the Atlas printed "Adas" in its own
--     Model Type line.
--   The Death's Head's Model Type prints AFC-O50 with a letter O; it is stored
--     AFC-050, as the Sky Cycle's AFC-023 prints a true zero.
--   The Atlas's Techno-Wizard Modifications block is not numbered by the book;
--     it is weapon row 4 so its four mechanics are not lost in a description.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('uar-1-enforcer', 'UAR-1 Enforcer Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One or two: a pilot and a co-pilot/gunner; the pilot can handle it alone.', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across; add 10 feet (3 m) with a running start.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 19 feet, 7 inches (6 m); Width: 12 feet (3.6 m); Length: 7 feet, 6 inches (2.3 m)', '18 tons fully loaded', 350, 1, NULL, 28000000, 'Black Market Cost: 28 million credits and up for a new, undamaged, fully powered Enforcer with rail gun and missiles. Eight to 10 million rebuilt, or without missiles and rail gun. Rare.', 'The Coalition''s Urban Assault Robot, a 20 foot (6.1 m) ground unit built for fighting inside cities; in service for more than 30 years by 109 P.A. and since 105 P.A. posted mostly to the ''Burbs and the lower city levels against riots, armed attacks and monsters. Robotic P.S. 40. Nuclear power, 20 year average life. Cargo is about three feet (0.9 m) of space behind the seats.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.249-250'),
('cr-003-spider-skull-walker', 'CR-003 Spider-Skull Walker', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One pilot and copilot.', 'Seats six additional passengers.', 'Running: 80 mph (128 km) maximum. Leaping is not possible.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 28 feet, 9 inches (8.8 m); Width: skull 13 feet (3.9 m), legs extend to about 20 feet (6 m); Length: skull 15 feet (4.5 m), about 18 feet (5.4 m) with the rail guns', '28 tons fully loaded', 500, 1, NULL, 36000000, 'Black Market Cost: 36 million credits and up for a new, undamaged, fully powered walker with full missile systems. Rare.', 'A six-legged Coalition all-terrain assault robot built around a giant skull, close to 30 feet (9.1 m) tall, quick over rubble and wreckage and able to climb 40 degree slopes. It serves as troop support, small squad transport, city defense and border patrol. Robotic P.S. 50. Nuclear power, 15 year average life. Cargo is roughly a 6x6x6 foot (1.8 m) hold plus a weapons locker holding six C-12 laser rifles, two C-14 Fire Breathers, one C-27 plasma rifle, one rocket launcher, 24 standard E-Clips, six Long-Clips, four Canister E-Clips and 12 fragmentation grenades.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.250-251'),
('cs-mark-v-apc', 'CS Mark V APC', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Five: pilot, copilot, communications, and two gunners.', 'Standard is 20 Dead Boy Grunts and six SAMAS, or four other power armor units and two hovercycles. A pair of SAMAS may be swapped for a pair of hover cycles or four soldiers in jet packs.', '90 mph (144 km) maximum on land.', NULL, 'About 30 mph (48 km).', 'Height: 16 feet, 8 inches (5.1 m); Width: 9 feet (2.7 m); Length: 33 feet, 6 inches (10.2 m)', '18 tons fully loaded', 350, 1, NULL, 21000000, 'Black Market Cost: 21 million credits and up for a new, undamaged, fully powered Coalition APC with rail gun and missiles. Eight to 10 million rebuilt, or without missiles and rail gun; three million rebuilt with no weapon systems at all. Seldom available.', 'The Coalition''s eight-wheeled Armored Personnel Carrier, an Infantry Assault and Transport Vehicle with thick armor and a great many guns, meant to drive troops into a combat zone and back out through whatever stands in the way. Nuclear power, 15 year average life. Cargo is about four feet (1.2 m) of space, plus locked overhead compartments holding 12 C-14 Fire Breathers, 12 C-12 laser rifles, four C-27 plasma rifles, four rocket launchers and 24 fragmentation mini-missiles.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.251-252'),
('afc-050-deaths-head-transport', 'AFC-050 Death''s Head Transport', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Nine: one pilot, one copilot, two gunners, two communication engineers, three technical officers.', 'Standard load is two APCs with their 20 troops each, two UAR-1 Enforcers, one Spider-Skull Walker, and 96 infantry soldiers (one third fewer if all are SAMAS). Without the vehicles and robots it holds approximately 384 soldiers and one Spider-Skull Walker.', 'Driving on the ground: not possible.', 'Hovers stationary up to 2000 feet (610 m) or flies. Maximum speed Mach One, about 670 mph (1072 km); cruising speed about 350 mph (560 km). Maximum altitude about 40,000 feet (12192 m). The jets must cool after at most twenty hours of flight above cruising speed; range is indefinite with rest stops and/or at cruising speed.', NULL, 'Height: 76 feet (23.2 m); Width: 104 feet (32.7 m); Length: 240 feet (73 m). The opening text calls it nearly 300 feet (91.5 m) long.', 'Approximately 1250 tons fully loaded', 1300, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market Cost: 300 million or more, but a Death''s Head Transport has never been available on the Black Market. No price is stored because none has ever been for sale.', 'The Coalition''s Air Armored Troop Carrier: a huge skull-fronted flying transport riding on a smaller saucer section that gives it full hover, VTOL and the ability to stop and spin in place. It is a delivery system for robots, power armor and infantry far more than an attacker, and also hauls cargo and runs rescue and support. The two sections can separate; the saucer drops or lands on autopilot, and the main body keeps its speed but then needs an airstrip and loses quick stops and spins. Nuclear power, 20 year average life. Stores normally include a dozen first-aid kits with RMK Robot Medical Kits, two weeks of food and water for 288 soldiers, 144 C-12 and 48 C-10 laser rifles, 96 C-14 Fire Breathers, 48 C-27 plasma rifles, 24 rocket launchers, 144 fragmentation mini-missiles, 1440 standard E-Clips, and usually a dozen SAMAS.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.252-253'),
('afc-023-sky-cycle', 'AFC-023 Sky Cycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One.', 'Can possibly seat one passenger, but it is dangerous and uncomfortable for the passenger.', '40 mph (64 km) maximum. Ground capability is limited to parking and maneuvering.', 'Hovers stationary up to 2000 feet (610 m) or flies. Maximum speed 520 mph (832 km); cruising speed between 80 and 150 mph (128 and 240 km). Maximum altitude about 5000 feet (1524 m). The jets must cool after at most 20 hours of continuous flight above cruising speed; range is indefinite with rest stops and/or at cruising speed.', NULL, 'Height: 10 feet (3 m); Width: 4 feet (1.2 m); Length: 9 feet, 4 inches (2.8 m)', 'One ton fully loaded', 150, 1, NULL, 1200000, 'Black Market Cost: 1.2 to 2 million credits. Rare.', 'The Coalition''s Air Urban Assault Vehicle, a fast one-man flyer that threads between buildings and trees and turns hard at almost any speed. It patrols the cities, the ''Burbs and the land around them and flies air support for CS infantry and reconnaissance teams. Nuclear power, 20 year average life. Cargo is three feet (0.9 m) of space behind the seat.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.253-254'),
('ng-x9-samson-power-armor', 'NG-X9 Samson Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 150 mph (240 km) maximum; running tires the operator at 10% of the usual fatigue rate. Leaping: 25 feet (7.6 m) high or across without the jet boosters; a booster-assisted leap reaches 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across. This is not flight.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 11 feet (3.3 m); Width: 5 feet (1.5 m); Length: 4 feet, 6 inches (1.4 m)', '460 lbs (207 kg) without rail gun and drum, 1000 pounds (450 kg) fully loaded', 240, 1, NULL, 850000, 'Black Market Cost: 850,000-950,000 credits for a new, undamaged, fully powered suit with rail gun and one full ammo-drum. Good availability; excellent in and around Michigan.', 'Northern Gun''s general-purpose combat and exploration suit, an Armored Infantry Assault Suit. It does not fly but makes thruster-assisted leaps, runs very fast and is a capable hand to hand fighter. Robotic P.S. 30. Nuclear power, 15 year average life. A small storage area takes extra supplies and personal weapons. The book pictures it on p.84.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.271-272'),
('ft-005-flying-titan-power-armor', 'FT-005 Flying Titan Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum; running tires the operator at 20% of the usual fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across without the thrusters; a thruster-assisted leap reaches 100 feet (30.5 m) high and 200 feet (61 m) across without actual flight.', 'Hovers stationary up to 200 feet (61 m) or flies. Maximum speed 400 mph (640 km); cruising speed 150 mph (240 km). Maximum altitude about 4000 feet (1219 m). The jets must cool after at most ten hours of continuous flight above cruising speed, or twenty hours at cruising speed; range is indefinite with periodic rest stops.', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.4 m), as printed; Width: 2.5 feet (0.76 m) wings down, 11 feet (3.3 m) wings extended; Length: about 3 feet (0.9 m)', '160 lbs (72 kg) without missiles', 180, 1, NULL, 1000000, 'Black Market Cost: One million credits for a new, undamaged, fully powered suit with missiles. Good availability.', 'A light, man-sized flying suit from the secretive Titan Industries, classed as a Strategic Armor Military Exoskeleton. Very fast and agile in the air and able to land and fight on foot, it suits reconnaissance, rescue and infantry support; it normally carries no rail gun, the pilot relying on energy rifles and wing missiles. Augmented P.S. 24 (same as a Juicer). Nuclear power, 20 year average life. No cargo space.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.272'),
('tr-001-titan-combat-robot', 'TR-001 Titan Combat Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One pilot.', 'Can accommodate two passengers.', 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or across; add 10 feet (3 m) with a running start.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 28 feet, 5 inches (8.6 m); Width: 15 feet (4.6 m); Length: 9 feet, 4 inches (2.8 m)', '22 tons fully loaded', 370, 1, NULL, 24000000, 'Black Market Cost: 24 million credits and up for a new model. 11 million rebuilt, or without missiles and rail gun. Fair availability of both.', 'The Combat Titan is a Ground/Infantry Assault Robot from Titan Industries, sturdy enough to stand up to a Coalition UAR-1 Enforcer. Expeditions heading into bandit country or lands held by demons and magic favor it. Robotic P.S. 36. Nuclear power, 15 year average life. Cargo is about four feet (1.2 m) of space.', 'Rifts Ultimate Edition p.273-274'),
('atlas-mark-i-assault-robot', 'Atlas Mark I Assault Robot', 'rifts', 'robot', 'One pilot/gunner; can accommodate a copilot and two gunners. Archimedes prefers to work alone, which reduces the number of attacks.', 'Seats three additional passengers.', 'Running: 70 mph (112 kmph) maximum.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 50 feet (15.2 m); Width: 23 feet (7 m); Length: 20 feet (6 m)', '50 tons fully loaded', 1000, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Black Market Cost: if the robot were ever mass-produced (unlikely) it would cost at least 500+ million credits. A unique prototype that cost the Olympian Club over a billion credits to develop; no price is stored because it is not for sale.', 'A one-of-a-kind giant robot built by Archimedes, weapon-smith of the Olympian Club, with help from Vulcan and Zeus the Thunderer; it marries advanced technology to techno-wizardry and is shaped and painted like a bearded marble Greek statue. Physical Strength equal to P.S. 60. Nuclear and magic power, 30 year average life. Six foot (1.8 m) cargo bay. Sealed for all environments, outer space and underwater included. The heading prints the model as "Adas Mark I".', 'Rifts Conversion Book Two: Pantheons of the Megaverse p.106-107'),
('ahriman-mark-i-rune-assault-suit', 'Ahriman Mark I Rune Assault Suit', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, '60 mph/96 km, and only because Ahriman partly drives the suit with his own supernatural strength.', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 12 feet tall (3.6 m); Width: 8 feet (2.4 m); Length: 4 feet (1.2 m)', NULL, 1800, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The personal prototype armor of the dark god Ahriman, made by demonic techno-wizardry: every piece is a living demon forced into inorganic shape. Black with red runes and styled after Coalition armor, it is form-fitting, so the wearer must stand ten feet (3 m) tall, and he cannot cast spells inside it. Sensors and life support are magical and keep working until the main body is destroyed. P.S. 45 (supernatural). Demon-powered, average energy 20 years.', 'Rifts Conversion Book Two: Pantheons of the Megaverse p.195');

